#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:5
#: cbac0fb82146409287ddb6ea224623ee
msgid "Kebni SensAItion External AHRS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:7
#: c61853fb1a59435fb47bd192b4549dd8
msgid "The Kebni SensAItion range includes three sensor models:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:9
#: 591a093b785242f3ac8a5ae33fde9a79
msgid "**IMU**: Measures acceleration, rotation (gyro rates), magnetic field and air pressure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:10
#: 3906344458934480b59eae6a2e85abab
msgid "**AHRS**: As above, but also estimates the orientation (roll, pitch and yaw/heading) of the sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:11
#: 223604dc5e4f405fad1c3dc02f83175d
msgid "**INS**: As above, but with two built-in satellite navigation receivers to get position (using Fixed Base RTK for higher precision if provided with correction data), UTC time and heading (if using two antennas with a sufficient baseline between them)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:13
#: e39a42b7dfd34307a6326f78a3bb1db8
msgid "The SensAItion range of sensors contain high-performance gyros and accelerometers that are individually calibrated and temperature compensated for the interval -40 to +70 :math:`^\\circ\\text{C}` and thus do not need any warm-up period to provide precise measurements. The built-in sensor fusion engine also uses a barometer and magnetometer to improve the estimation of altitude and heading, respectively. The INS version of the sensor further includes satellite positioning in the sensor fusion, with precise internal synchronization between the satellite position fixes and the IMU measurements to get the best performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:20
#: b692bd466f95417eb64c45f6cc7b8bdf
msgid "For easier integration into various customer applications, each model exists in two hardware versions: a rugged version in an IP67 aluminium housing or a low-profile OEM version that can easily be mounted on an application-specific circuit board. Details and specifications for each model can be found on `Kebni's product homepage <https://www.kebni.com/products/inertial-sensing/sensaition-imu-ins/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:25
#: 5ffd0ee24b5e49c89c6babbd725409c3
msgid "The SensAItion External AHRS driver can work in two modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:27
#: 54cfaf13bd1547deb910719eeae23658
msgid "**IMU**: It should be connected to the IMU or AHRS model of SensAItion and will feed raw sensor data to the ArduPilot EKF3 estimator, which will fuse it with GPS positions from another source and compute a navigation solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:28
#: 46938836c4a9471ba9fe009968bfd9a3
msgid "**Interleaved INS**: It should be connected to the INS model of SensAItion, which will run sensor fusion and provide a full navigation solution, replacing the EKF3 estimator. In order not to overload the serial port, the high-rate IMU messages are interleaved with lower-rate positions and orientations. This interleaving requires the sensor to have firmware version 2.69 or newer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:31
#: 0bb25a516c514229a6920d9e7d93dd45
msgid "Hardware setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:32
#: 6dd5550e9ac14f0187432946902ad579
msgid "Connect the SensAItion Data UART pins (TX, RX and ground) to an available serial port on the ArduPilot platform, such as GPS or TELEM. Power the sensor as described in the User Manual. Both the rugged and OEM version of the sensor have the required serial port connections available. Please note that the rugged sensor version has output voltage levels +/-5 V, while the OEM sensor version has output voltage levels of 0 and +3.3 V."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:38
#: 7729e7f0f5ce4802bbcfa2fcbc3612b3
msgid "The SensAItion sensor can be mounted in any orientation and the output can be rotated to match the local coordinate system if needed - see the configuration section below. As with any IMU, it is important to avoid excessive vibration levels and it is beneficial to use a mechanical damper between the sensor and the platform frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:44
#: 0c3e09c28f3c4f01b32d385b22ef11dd
msgid "Configuration of the sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:45
#: 33f1e2d313b44e2191204d47f83c6177
msgid "The SensAItion sensor has a number of configuration registers that control the baudrate, output data format, coordinate system rotation and much more. The configuration registers can be read and written using a text-based protocol via the User UART port as described in the User Manual. But Kebni also provides, on request, the Kebni INSight graphical user interface that helps the user set all configuration registers and can also be used to read and plot sensor data and perform a magnetometer calibration. For complete control of the sensor configuration, it is recommended to use INSight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:52
#: a1f2495e8e2946c998b80c208dbf16e2
msgid "Contact `Kebni <https://www.kebni.com/contact/>`__ for access to the User Manual or Kebni INSight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-ahrs-sensaition.rst:54
#: dfc669fed56447cfb0ad5b6c53f494b1
